"synonyms":[]},"Raymond":{"id":"96eadf54-7402-4109-9a63-980566c753e3","word":"Raymond","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"male given name","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Raimundo"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"An uncle of mine whose name was Cecil Jeffery Courtenay obtained a post of great emolument simply by virtue of his 'pretty' name. Mine, I think, is quite as effective, though it depends upon but one Christian name, Raymond. I am Raymond Courtenay.","ref":"1886 Mary Elizabeth Braddon: Belgravia Magazine. Item notes:V.60.(July-Oct.1886) page 94","id":"22990c9d-83d2-4114-9c57-d4098f88ce99"},{"text":"What splendid names for boys there are! / There's Carol like a rolling car, / And Martin like a flying bird, / And Adam like the Lord's First Word, / And Raymond like the Harvest Moon,","ref":"1933, Eleanor Farjeon, “Boys' Names”, in Over the Garden Wall, Faber and Faber, page 90:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[154,161]],"id":"dc568c5f-d194-41b7-999b-4685718cd214"},{"text":"I thought the name Raymond sounded respectable. Good name for a lawyer.","ref":"2006, Janette McCarthy, Hanging on a String, →ISBN, page 141:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[19,26]],"id":"c4462e05-5ad7-42b5-9ae7-3cfe345f7b98"},{"text":"A spokesperson for the families of Drs. Mortimer and Raymond Sackler, the late founders of the company, issued this statement:","ref":"2019 March 24, Ralph Ellis and Melanie Schuman, “Hundreds of cities, counties and Native American tribes file federal lawsuit against Sackler family over opioid crisis”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[53,60]],"id":"39d68ea6-54c8-4938-8fec-1ce020e4c3ce"}],"categories":["English given names","English male given names","English male given names from Germanic languages","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["given name","given name"]],"glosses":["A male given name from the Germanic languages."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"